  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3227.06 Emergency Brakes",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3227.06 Emergency Brakes.\n\n(a) A trailer shall be rejected if:\n\n(1) The emergency brakes do not automatically apply when the breakaway safety mechanism is operated; or\n\n(2) The emergency brakes do not release when the breakaway safety mechanism is returned to the normal position.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16 (from Saf-C 3227.07)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
